WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.260
The murderous robot with the killer&nbsp;
dance moves, also known as M3GAN,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:09.660
is coming to a theater near you. But can the&nbsp;
android antagonist live up to all the viral hype?

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:15.120
M3GAN tells the story of a young girl, Cady,&nbsp;
who loses both of her parents in a horrible&nbsp;accident.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:20.280
She's adopted by her aunt, Gemma, a&nbsp;
woman who isn't quite prepared to take on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:25.740
responsibility of a child, let alone one who's&nbsp;
been as traumatized as Cady. To help the young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.880
girl cope with the loss of her family and&nbsp;
the repercussions of being isolated at such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:35.160
a young age, Gemma — who earns her living&nbsp;
as a roboticist — introduces her niece to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:40.200
project she's been working on. This project is&nbsp;
a "toy" that can act as a child's best friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.760
a companion that's supposed to chase away&nbsp;
loneliness or any other negative emotion.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:51.600
Gemma calls this toy Model Three Generative&nbsp;
Android, aka M3GAN. Once the two are introduced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:57.000
to one another, Cady becomes very attached to&nbsp;
the eerily lifelike doll. M3GAN seems to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.860
capable of free will so long as her decisions&nbsp;
are always in service to her mission — to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:07.260
protect Cady and ensure that she's always happy.&nbsp;
However, as Cady grows more attached to M3GAN,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:12.540
there are concerns of her becoming too codependent&nbsp;
on the android. But when you've got an advanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:17.100
piece of machinery like M3GAN running around,&nbsp;
codependency is the least of your concerns.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:22.440
M3GAN becomes increasingly aggressive in her&nbsp;
pursuit of caring for Cady, ignoring commands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:27.900
from the woman who created her and even attacking&nbsp;
a child she catches harassing Cady. M3GAN looks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.280
be a growing problem throughout the film,&nbsp;
with her fierce protectiveness spiraling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:37.392
into outright murder, setting up a showdown&nbsp;
between Cady, Gemma, and the killer doll.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:44.520
M3GAN set the world on fire with its phenomenal&nbsp;
trailer, which dropped on October 11, 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:49.560
attracting nearly 20 million views. The&nbsp;
highlight moment of the trailer, where M3GAN&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.720
shows off her dancing abilities while pursuing&nbsp;
her prey, even inspired all sorts of memes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:59.880
while prompting fans to recreate the killer&nbsp;
robot's killer dance moves. In other words,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.980
it seems the world has M3GAN fever, and we expect&nbsp;
the film to make a killing at the box office.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.960
And yeah, we said "box office." Unlike&nbsp;
other films — like Halloween Ends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:15.300
which hit both Peacock and theater screens at the&nbsp;
same time — it seems like M3GAN will exclusively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:20.160
be playing on the big screen. While the film was&nbsp;
originally scheduled for a January 13th release,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:26.760
M3GAN will now dance its way into theaters&nbsp;
on January 6, 2023, where it will no doubt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:31.800
inspire even more memes and hopefully just&nbsp;
as many screams. In addition to all the free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:37.020
online publicity created by Twitter and TikTok&nbsp;
users, M3GAN has been getting plenty of attention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:43.140
thanks to the titular character's online war of&nbsp;
words with the OG murder doll himself, Chucky.

00:02:43.608 --> 00:02:46.848
"Hi, I'm Chucky. Wanna play?"

00:02:46.848 --> 00:02:51.180
The former Charles Lee Ray has had quite&nbsp;
a lot to say about M3GAN's existence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:56.460
but M3GAN has done a pretty good job of clapping&nbsp;
back on Twitter. Having these characters beef&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.460 --> 00:03:01.320
with one another as if they were real entities&nbsp;
has only added to the press revolving around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:06.960
the pair of killer dolls, and it's shining a&nbsp;
light on both M3GAN and Syfy's TV show Chucky.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:10.260
When it comes to the character of Gemma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:14.580
the filmmakers behind M3GAN decided to cast&nbsp;
someone who's no stranger to frightening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:19.860
films. The protagonist is played by Allison&nbsp;
Williams, perhaps best known to horror fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:25.740
as the disturbing, manipulative, milk-loving&nbsp;
Rose from Get Out. She also starred in one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:31.680
Netflix's most upsetting movies, the controversial&nbsp;
body horror film The Perfection. Needless to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:35.820
Gemma will be a far different character&nbsp;
from Get Out's Rose. She appears to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:39.480
be a loving but ill-equipped aunt&nbsp;
who's doing her best to help Cady,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:43.740
even if that does involve inadvertently&nbsp;
unleashing a murder droid upon the world.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:49.080
As for poor Cady, that part will be played&nbsp;
by the incredibly talented Violet McGraw,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:53.640
a young actor who has plenty of horror&nbsp;
experience herself. She starred as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:57.540
young version of Nell in Mike Flanagan's&nbsp;
Netflix series The Haunting of Hill House,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:01.620
and she collaborated with the director&nbsp;
again in Doctor Sleep, where she played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:05.940
the young girl in the opening of the film who&nbsp;
falls prey to the vampiric True Knot clan.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:11.940
But who's playing the titular killer doll herself?&nbsp;
Well, the role will go to two different actors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:16.620
Jenna Davis will be voicing M3GAN, and you&nbsp;
may know her from series like Raven's Home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:21.120
Scarlett's Lab, and Treehouse Detectives.&nbsp;
While Davis will be delivering the lines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:27.240
Amie Donald will actually play M3GAN. The young&nbsp;
actress only has one credit to date — she was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:32.700
in Netflix's Sweet Tooth — but she's a talented&nbsp;
dancer who was trained for the role by Luke Hawker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:38.490
and Jed Brophy, two actors who specialize in&nbsp;
playing creepy creatures with strange movements.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:43.260
With the emergence of filmmakers&nbsp;
like Jordan Peele and Zach Cregger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:48.240
there seems to be a trend of comedians shifting&nbsp;
their talents over to horror. It honestly makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:52.740
a lot of sense when you think about it. As&nbsp;
horror author Joe R. Lansdale once put it,

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:08.868
"Is that so?" "Yes. Experts&nbsp;
say—" "M3GAN, turn off."

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:14.100
When it comes to this trend of funny filmmakers&nbsp;
going in a scarier direction, we also have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:18.720
bring up director Gerard Johnstone, the man&nbsp;
behind M3GAN. Johnstone's roots are in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:24.300
world of New Zealand comedy, as he worked on TV&nbsp;
shows like The Jaquie Brown Diaries, Terry Teo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:30.000
and The New Legends of Monkey. However,&nbsp;
in 2014, he began to get a bit spookier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.220
with his first feature film, the horror-comedy&nbsp;
Housebound, a film inspired by Ghosthunters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:38.940
where a dysfunctional family must deal&nbsp;
with the spirits inhabiting their home.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:44.460
Johnstone earned quite a few award nominations for&nbsp;
his work on Housebound from the likes of Fangoria,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:51.120
Fright Meter, and the SXSW Film Festival, with&nbsp;
his movie winning best feature at the Neuchâtel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.560
International Fantastic Film Festival.&nbsp;
And now, Johnstone is returning to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.560 --> 00:06:00.720
horror genre with M3GAN. While it might not be&nbsp;
uproariously funny like some of his early works,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:05.040
it definitely seems like it's going to go&nbsp;
in some bizarre and humorous directions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:09.960
especially when it comes to M3GAN's ability&nbsp;
to boogie while murdering everyone in sight.

00:06:10.857 --> 00:06:12.840
One of the reasons horror fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:17.400
are so excited about M3GAN is because&nbsp;
of who's penning the screenplay. Akela&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:21.720
Cooper has been busy in the writing world for&nbsp;
quite a while, working on shows like Grimm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:27.240
The 100, and Luke Cage. Her first script to&nbsp;
be turned into a feature film was Hell Fest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:32.880
the 2018 story of a slasher on the loose&nbsp;
at a horror-themed amusement park. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:36.240
it was her next feature film that&nbsp;
would truly put Cooper on the map.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:39.060
In 2021, viewers were treated to Malignant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:44.760
an absolutely bonkers horror movie directed by&nbsp;
James Wan. If you haven't seen Malignant yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:50.160
stop what you're doing and check it out. A&nbsp;
film that feels like Dario Argento mashed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:55.680
up with Chad Stahelski, Malignant was one of the&nbsp;
craziest horror films in years, and those who dug&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:00.660
its bizarro vibe are incredibly psyched to see&nbsp;
what weirdness Cooper has cooked up this time.

00:07:01.674 --> 00:07:03.000
Speaking of Malignant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:08.220
that film was helmed by the one and only James&nbsp;
Wan, the horror legend known for the creation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:13.020
of The Conjuring, the first two Insidious&nbsp;
films, and the original Saw. With Wan's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:17.340
involvement as a producer on M3GAN, it's no&nbsp;
wonder that people have been comparing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:22.320
2023 film to Malignant, especially thanks&nbsp;
to the similarities between the complex,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:27.900
Matrix-like choreography displayed in Malignant&nbsp;
and the unnatural way in which M3GAN moves.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:33.720
Of course, Wan isn't the only terrifying titan&nbsp;
producing this upcoming flick. Jason Blum,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:39.300
the man behind Blumhouse Productions, is also&nbsp;
co-producing the film. Blumhouse's fingerprints&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:44.400
are all over the modern-day horror genre, as&nbsp;
the banner has released incredibly scary and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:49.980
influential movies like Get Out, The Invisible&nbsp;
Man, Split, and long-running series like The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:54.540
Purge, Insidious, and Paranormal Activity.&nbsp;
With these two powerhouses behind the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:59.394
M3GAN is already gearing up to be a wild&nbsp;
ride that has fans buzzing with excitement.

00:08:00.311 --> 00:08:03.000
When it comes to ratings, quite a few horror films&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:09.240
boast the big, bad R. Some recent examples include&nbsp;
slasher flick Halloween Ends, the incredibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:15.120
freaky Smile, and Jordan Peele's sci-fi adventure&nbsp;
Nope. However, some of the scariest horror movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:21.960
of all time are rated PG-13. A Quiet Place, Drag&nbsp;
Me to Hell, and Scary Stories to Tell in the Dark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:27.360
all carry the more family-friendly rating,&nbsp;
and they're all straight-up nightmare fuel.

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:33.300
Blumhouse Productions also has quite a few&nbsp;
frightening PG-13 films, such as James Wan's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:39.120
Insidious and M. Night Shyamalan's Split. And&nbsp;
now, it looks like M3GAN is joining Blumhouse's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:45.060
PG-13 pantheon. According to FilmRatings.com,&nbsp;
the upcoming robo-thriller earned the rating for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:49.380
"violent content and terror, some strong&nbsp;
language, and a suggestive reference."

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:52.860
As it looks like M3GAN is going&nbsp;
to go on a murder rampage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:57.780
we're assuming that's where the violent content&nbsp;
and terror come from, and we're assuming some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:01.680
frightened victim is going to drop a few&nbsp;
harsh words here and there. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:06.180
with a PG-13 rating, while it might not&nbsp;
pack the gore of a Michael Myers movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:11.040
M3GAN is sure to draw in a wider audience&nbsp;
and earn those big box office dollars.

00:09:12.035 --> 00:09:14.280
We know what you're thinking: How can you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:19.560
ask if there's going to be a M3GAN sequel when the&nbsp;
film hasn't even hit theaters yet? It does seem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:24.840
a strange question on the surface, but really,&nbsp;
it shouldn't be all that surprising. We live in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:30.240
a world dominated by intellectual property, or IP&nbsp;
— where studios are always on the lookout for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:35.432
next big franchise. And it seems like the folks&nbsp;
at Universal think they've found one with M3GAN.

00:09:35.432 --> 00:09:37.736
"It's honestly like she's part of the family now."

00:09:37.736 --> 00:09:42.180
While Blumhouse is the production company&nbsp;
behind M3GAN, Universal is distributing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:45.960
horror film. In an article detailing&nbsp;
the very real possibility of Jason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:49.980
Blum and James Wan combining their&nbsp;
production companies — Blumhouse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:54.540
and Atomic Monster — into one horror&nbsp;
monolith, The New York Times reported,

00:10:06.635 --> 00:10:11.880
So it looks like a M3GAN sequel might be in the&nbsp;
pipeline. That leaves us to wonder, will M3GAN&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:17.520
survive the original film? Will she kill off the&nbsp;
human protagonists? Or will she be defeated and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:23.220
then rise from the grave, Chucky-style? We&nbsp;
can't wait to find out on January 6, 2023.

